  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Banker Card**: The banker turns up one card from the deck and places it on their right (The Banker's Card). 2. **Player Card**: The banker turns up a second card and places it on the left (The Player's Card). 3. **Initial Tie**: If these two cards match in rank, the banker wins all bets immediately. 4. **The Draw**: The banker continues turning up cards from the deck one by one. - If a card matches the Banker's Card rank, the banker wins all bets. - If a card matches the Player's Card rank, the banker pays all bettors at even money.",
    Player: "1. **Banker Card**: The banker turns up one card from the deck and places it on their right (The Banker's Card). 2. **Player Card**: The banker turns up a second card and places it on the left (The Player's Card). 3. **Initial Tie**: If these two cards match in rank, the banker wins all bets immediately. 4. **The Draw**: The banker continues turning up cards from the deck one by one. - If a card matches the Banker's Card rank, the banker wins all bets. - If a card matches the Player's Card rank, the banker pays all bettors at even money.",
    objective: "Bet on whether the 'Player' card or the 'Banker' card will appear first as cards are turned up from the deck.",
    gameplay: "1. **Banker Card**: The banker turns up one card from the deck and places it on their right (The Banker's Card). 2. **Player Card**: The banker turns up a second card and places it on the left (The Player's Card). 3. **Initial Tie**: If these two cards match in rank, the banker wins all bets immediately. 4. **The Draw**: The banker continues turning up cards from the deck one by one. - If a card matches the Banker's Card rank, the banker wins all bets. - If a card matches the Player's Card rank, the banker pays all bettors at even money.",
    keyRules: [
      'Only card ranks matter; suits are irrelevant.',
      'If the first two cards match (tie), banker wins immediately.',
      'The first matching card dealt determines the winner.',
      'Bets are typically placed after seeing the first two cards but before the draw begins.',
      'Multiple decks reduce the frequency of ties.',
